---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { factIssuerCount } from '../lib/facts.mjs';

const issuerCount = factIssuerCount();

const lastReviewed = '2026-11-11';
const siteOrigin = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL || 'https://defycard.com';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: `${siteOrigin}/` },
  { name: 'About', url: `${siteOrigin}/about/` },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About DefyCard — independent crypto card comparisons"
  description={`DefyCard is an independent crypto debit and credit card comparison hub. Issuer facts for ${issuerCount} issuers are kept as dated records with a verification date, an expiry and a source link.`}
  activeNav="cards"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1>About DefyCard</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      DefyCard is an independent comparison hub for crypto debit and credit cards.
      We exist because the marketing pages of card issuers, while technically
      accurate, make it almost impossible to compare them on the things that
      actually matter to you: cashback that survives the FX fee, custody you
      retain after the card ships, and country availability that holds for the
      jurisdiction you spend in.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <p>
      For each
      card we maintain an internal record covering cashback structure, foreign
      exchange spread, top-up rails, custody model, regulatory status, and the
      country and US-state availability matrix. The country availability matrix
      is compared with the issuer’s own list daily. Issuer facts live in dated
      fact records, each with a verification date, an expiry and a source link,
      for {issuerCount} issuers. Figures for other cards carry the date printed
      next to them.
    </p>

    <h2>Methodology</h2>
    <p>
      How a figure gets onto a page and what our labels mean:
      <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <p>
      DefyCard is not a Crypto Asset Service Provider. We do not custody funds,
      operate an exchange, run a wallet, or hold any license to sell financial
      products. We do not provide investment, tax, or legal advice; nothing on
      this site is a recommendation to buy, sell, or hold any digital asset.
      Card issuers, not DefyCard, are responsible for KYC, settlement, and
      regulatory compliance with respect to any account you open through our
      links.
    </p>

    <h2>How we sustain the work</h2>
    <p>
      DefyCard earns affiliate commissions when readers sign up for a card
      through our referral links. Commissions never alter scoring rank, never
      grant an issuer rewrite rights over a published article, and never gate
      a critical finding behind a payment. The
      <a href="/disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a> page explains the
      mechanics, the partners, and the firewall between revenue and editorial.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial policy</h2>
    <p>
      Who edits the site and how to send a correction:
      <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="page-meta">Last updated: {lastReviewed}</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .legal-page h2 {
    margin-top: 1.8em;
  }
  .legal-page p {
    color: var(--on-surface);
    margin: 0 0 1em;
  }
  .page-meta {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }
</style>
